{"name":"Pink Panther","hex":"#ff0090","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"panther","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various big cats with black fur; most especially, the black-coated leopard of Africa and Asia.","Any big cat of the genus Panthera."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panther"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pink Panther (character)","blocks":[{"text":"The Pink Panther is a fictional animated character who appears in the opening or closing credit sequences of every film in The Pink Panther series. In the storyline of the original film, \"Pink Panther\" is the name of a valuable pink diamond named for a flaw that shows a \"figure of a springing panther\" when held up to the light in a certain way; in the credits, the diamond is personified by an animated, anthropomorphic panther with pink fur. In the original film series, only the first Pink Panther film and its sequel, The Return of the Pink Panther, featured the diamond."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/96/Pink_Panther.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Panther_(character)","wikidata":"Q15012089"},{"title":"The Pink Panther","blocks":[{"text":"The Pink Panther is an American media franchise primarily focusing on a series of comedy-mystery films featuring an inept French police detective, Inspector Jacques Clouseau, as well as an animated series created by DePatie–Freleng Enterprises about the titular Pink Panther character. The franchise began with the release of the film The Pink Panther in 1963 and the animated cartoons began in 1964 with the short film The Pink Phink."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pink_Panther","wikidata":"Q7143846"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/The_Pink_Panther_in_The_Pink_Panther_trailer_%281963%29_04.png/330px-The_Pink_Panther_in_The_Pink_Panther_trailer_%281963%29_04.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/The_Pink_Panther_in_The_Pink_Panther_trailer_%281963%29_04.png/330px-The_Pink_Panther_in_The_Pink_Panther_trailer_%281963%29_04.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The Pink Panther in the trailer of The Pink Panther (1963)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Pink_Panther_in_The_Pink_Panther_trailer_(1963)_04.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pink_Panther_Coruna.jpg/500px-Pink_Panther_Coruna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pink_Panther_Coruna.jpg/500px-Pink_Panther_Coruna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Engraving of the Pink Panther in A Coruña, Spain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_Panther_Coruna.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co